f Service cite4†Request an API Key cite5†Developers' Forum cite6†Geography cite7†Contact Us L59: \nL60: cite1†View All Available APIs L61: \nL62: * * *\nL63: \nL64: * * *\nL65: \nL66: cite8†Guidance for Developers cite9†Census Data API User Guide cite10†Census Microdata API User Guide cite11†Census Data API Discovery Tool cite12†Workshop: Basics of Using the Census API cite13†View All Video Tutorials L67: \nL68: * * *\nL69: \nL70: cite14†Latest Data Releases cite15†News cite16†Updates cite7†Contact Us L71: # International Trade (monthly 2010-present)\nL72: \nL73: cite0†Skip Navigation L74: \nL75: cite17†Within Developers L76: \nL77:   * cite2†About L78:   * cite1†Available APIs L79:   * cite5†Developers' Forum L80:   * cite6†Geography L81:   * cite8†Guidance for Developers L82:   * cite15†News L83:   * cite18†Terms of Service L84:   * cite16†Updates L85: \nL86: Within Developers\nL87: \nL88: cite17†Within Developers L89: \nL90:   * cite2†About L91:   * cite1†Available APIs L92:   * cite5†Developers' Forum L93:   * cite6†Geography L94:   * cite8†Guidance for Developers L95:   * cite15†News L96:   * cite18†Terms of Service L97:   * cite16†Updates L98: \nL99: ####\nL100: # International Trade (monthly 2010-present)\nL101: \nL102: April 07, 2026\nL103: \nL104: #### Time Series Data\nL105: \nL106: The International Trade datasets provide detailed up-to-date trade data between the United States and its international trade partners. The most current monthly and annual trade statistics are available in these datasets, which are updated monthly on the day of press release.\nL107: \nL108: \nL109: \nL110: #### Monthly International Trade Datasets (January 2010 – present)\nL111: ####\nL112: \nL113: The Monthly International Trade Timeseries Datasets provide the most comprehensive current month and cumulative year-to-date export and import statistics using multiple commodity classification systems. The Monthly International Trade Datasets currently have statistics from January 2010 to present. Previously released trade data are revised annually with the publication of April statistics.\nL114: ## Exports\nL115: \nL116:   * * * *\nL117: \nL118: cite19†Monthly U.S. Exports by Harmonized System (HS) Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/hs†api.census.gov L119: \nL120: * * *\nL121: \nL122:   * * * *\nL123: \nL124: cite20†Monthly U.S. Exports by North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/naics†api.census.gov L125: \nL126: * * *\nL127: \nL128:   * * * *\nL129: \nL130: cite21†Monthly U.S. Exports by End-use Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/enduse†api.census.gov L131: \nL132: * * *\nL133: \nL134:   * * * *\nL135: cite22†Monthly U.S. Exports by Standard International Trade Classification (SITC) Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/sitc†api.census.gov L136: \nL137: * * *\nL138: \nL139:   * * * *\nL140: \nL141: cite23†Monthly U.S. Exports by Department of Agriculture Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/usda†api.census.gov L142: \nL143: * * *\nL144: \nL145:   * * * *\nL146: \nL147: cite24†Monthly U.S. Exports by Advanced Technology Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/hitech†api.census.gov L148: \nL149: * * *\nL150: \nL151:   * * * *\nL152: cite25†Monthly U.S. Exports by State and Harmonized System (HS) Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/statehs†api.census.gov L153: \nL154: * * *\nL155: \nL156:   * * * *\nL157: \nL158: cite26†Monthly U.S. Exports by State and North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/statenaics†api.census.gov L159: \nL160: * * *\nL161: \nL162:   * * * *\nL163: \nL164: cite27†Monthly U.S. Exports by Port and Harmonized System (HS) Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/porths†api.census.gov L165: \nL166: * * *\nL167: ## Imports\nL168: \nL169:   * * * *\nL170: \nL171: cite28†Monthly U.S. Imports by Harmonized System (HS) Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/hs†api.census.gov L172: \nL173: * * *\nL174: \nL175:   * * * *\nL176: \nL177: cite29†Monthly U.S. Imports by North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/naics†api.census.gov L178: \nL179: * * *\nL180: \nL181:   * * * *\nL182: \nL183: cite30†Monthly U.S. Imports by End-use Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/enduse†api.census.gov L184: \nL185: * * *\nL186: \nL187:   * * * *\nL188: cite31†Monthly U.S. Imports by Standard International Trade Classification (SITC) Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/sitc†api.census.gov L189: \nL190: * * *\nL191: \nL192:   * * * *\nL193: \nL194: cite32†Monthly U.S. Imports by Department of Agriculture Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/usda†api.census.gov L195: \nL196: * * *\nL197: \nL198:   * * * *\nL199: \nL200: cite33†Monthly U.S. Imports by Advanced Technology Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/hitech†api.census.gov L201: \nL202: * * *\nL203: \nL204:   * * * *\nL205: cite34†Monthly U.S. Imports by State and Harmonized System (HS) Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/statehs†api.census.gov L206: \nL207: * * *\nL208: \nL209:   * * * *\nL210: \nL211: cite35†Monthly U.S. Imports by State and North American Industry Classification System (NAICS) api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/statenaics†api.census.gov L212: \nL213: * * *\nL214: \nL215:   * * * *\nL216: \nL217: cite36†Monthly U.S. Imports by Port and Harmonized System (HS) Code api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/porths†api.census.gov L218: \nL219: * * *\nL220: ### User Manual\nL221: \nL222: cite37†Download Guide to Using U.S. International Trade Datasets in the Census API [PDF - 1.8 MB] L223: \nL224: For a detailed guide on how to use the International Trade Datasets in the Census API, visit the Guide to International Trade Datasets.\nL225: \nL226:   * * * *\nL227: cite38†International Trade API Query Builder Tool The International Trade API Query Builder is a live-connection graphical user interface to the International Trade endpoints in the Census API. Because the tool only retrieves data when prompted it has no default settings and needs a user to provide inputs at each stage to function properly. To new users of the API, this tool is an easy method to build an API call. For more experienced users this tool is an effective shortcut. L228: \nL229: * * *\nL230: ### Data Collection & Methodology\nL231: \nL232: Data on U.S. exports of merchandise from the U.S. to all countries, except Canada, are compiled from the Electronic Export Information (EEI) filed by the U.S. Principle Party of Interest or their agents through the U.S. Customs' Automated Commercial Environment (ACE). Filing the EEI is mandatory under Chapter 9, Title 13, United States Code. Qualified exporters, or their agents, submit EEI data by automated means directly to the U.S. Census Bureau.\nL233: Data on U.S. imports of merchandise are compiled primarily from automated data submitted through the U.S. Customs' Automated Commercial Environment (ACE). Other sources of import data include import entry summary forms, warehouse withdrawal forms and Foreign Trade Zone documents. Data on imports of electricity and natural gas from Canada are obtained from Canadian sources.\nL234: \nL235: For more information on U.S. international trade data collection and methodology, visit:\nL236: \nL237:   * * * *\nL238: cite39†Guide to International Trade Statistics L239: \nL240: * * *\nL241: \nL242:   * * * *\nL243: \nL244: cite40†International Trade Program The official U.S. import and export statistics reflect both government and nongovernment shipments of merchandise between foreign countries and the U.S. L245: \nL246: * * *\nL247: \nL248: All data queries to the Census Data API now require an API key. Please cut and paste the Example Calls below into your web browser and replace YOUR_KEY_GOES_HERE with your personal API Key.\nL249: If you do not have an API Key, request one cite41†here†api.census.gov . For more information: cite42†Watch Video .\nL250: ### Monthly International Trade Time Series - Exports\nL251:   * API Call: cite19†api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/hs†api.census.gov L252:   * Examples: cite43†api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/hs/examples.html†api.census.gov L253:   * Geographies: cite44†api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/hs/geography.html†api.census.gov L254:   * Variables: cite45†api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/hs/variables.html†api.census.gov L255:   * Example Call: Shows the total export value and vessel export value from the district of Baltimore for all harmonized codes for December 2013\nL256: api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/hs?get=DISTRICT,DIST_NAME,E_COMMODITY,E_COMMODITY_LDESC,ALL_VAL_MO,ALL_VAL_YR,VES_VAL_MO,VES_VAL_YR&YEAR=2013&MONTH=12&DISTRICT=13&key=YOUR_KEY_GOES_HERE\nL257: \nL258:   * Example Call: Shows the year-to-date total, vessel, and air export value and year-to-date card count for every HS code for April 2013\nL259: \nL260: api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/exports/hs?get=E_COMMODITY,E_COMMODITY_LDESC,ALL_VAL_YR,VES_VAL_YR,AIR_VAL_YR,CC_YR&YEAR=2013&MONTH=04&key=YOUR_KEY_GOES_HERE\nL261: ### Monthly International Trade Time Series - Imports\nL262:   * API Call: cite30†api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/enduse†api.census.gov L263:   * Examples: cite46†api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/enduse/examples.html†api.census.gov L264:   * Geographies: cite47†api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/enduse/geography.html†api.census.gov L265:   * Variables: cite48†api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/enduse/variables.html†api.census.gov L266:   * Example Call: Shows the general imports value and imports for consumption value for all End-use codes and all countries for January 2013\nL267: api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/enduse?get=CTY_CODE,CTY_NAME,I_ENDUSE,I_ENDUSE_LDESC,GEN_VAL_MO,CON_VAL_MO&time=2013-01&key=YOUR_KEY_GOES_HERE\nL268: \nL269:   * Example Call: Shows the general imports value and imports for consumption value of cocoa beans from Ghana in February 2013\nL270: \nL271: api.census.gov/data/timeseries/intltrade/imports/enduse?get=CTY_CODE,CTY_NAME,I_ENDUSE,I_ENDUSE_LDESC,GEN_VAL_MO,CON_VAL_MO&I_ENDUSE=00010&CTY_CODE=7490&YEAR=2013&MONTH=02&key=YOUR_KEY_GOES_HERE\nL272: Page Last Revised - May 20, 2026\nL273: \nL274: Some content on this site is available in several different electronic formats. Some of the files may require a plug-in or additional software to view.\nL275: \nL276: ✕\nL277: \nL278: Is this page helpful?\nL279: cite49†Image: Thumbs Up Image†census.gov Yes cite50†Image: Thumbs Down Image†census.gov No\nL280: \nL281: ✕\nL282: \nL283: [Input]\nL284: \nL285: NO THANKS\nL286: \nL287: 255 characters maximum cite51†Image†census.gov 255 characters maximum reached\nL288: \nL289: ✕\nL290: \nL291: Thank you for your feedback.\nL292: Comments or suggestions? cite52†Image†census.gov cite53†Image†census.gov L293: \nL294: Top\nL295: cite54†Back to Header L296: \nL297: Receive Updates\nL298: \nL299: To sign up for updates please enter your email address.\nL300: \nL301: * * *\nL302: \nL303: Stay Current\nL304: \nL305: cite55†America Counts cite56†Director’s Blog cite57†Deputy Director’s Blog cite58†Random Samplings cite59†Research Matters L306: \nL307: Stay Connected\nL308: \nL309: cite60†Contact cite61†Support cite62†Jobs L310: \nL311: Follow\nL312: cite63†Information Quality | cite64†Data Linkage Infrastructure | cite65†Data Pro